{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>And they shall know</b> — Some say that a vav is missing from 'your name.' What seems right to me: that a shin is missing, serving in place of אשר, and so it reads: וידעו כי אתה שמך ה' לבדך ('and they shall know that you, whose name is YHWH, alone'). Likewise: 'Do not speak much, high things, and let us know — they are pursued and exalted, in contrast to their lightness.'"], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 83, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:35:58.337893008Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}